    level: 'intermediate',
    content: 'Bloom Filters (BIP37) are probabilistic data structures used by SPV wallets to request only relevant transactions from full nodes, without downloading the full blockchain. Criticized for severe privacy leaks. Key points: A BIP37 client sends a Bloom filter to a full node, which responds with matching Merkle blocks. Reduces bandwidth and RAM for mobile/SPV wallets compared to full node sync. **Privacy problem**: the filter reveals user addresses and transaction patterns to the queried full node. Some nodes disable BIP37 serving (\`peerbloomfilters=0\`) due to DoS and privacy concerns. Superseded by Compact Block Filters (BIP158/BIP157) as the privacy-preserving alternative. Why it matters: Bloom Filters illustrate the tension between SPV usability and privacy. Their failure drove development of BIP158, now the standard for lightweight wallet privacy.',
