    content: 'This investigation explores one of the internet\'s greatest unsolved mysteries: the identity of Satoshi Nakamoto, Bitcoin\'s anonymous creator. The story begins in the 1990s with the Cypherpunks-cryptographers seeking to build a decentralized, government-free digital currency. After earlier attempts failed, Satoshi published Bitcoin\'s whitepaper on October 31, 2008, during the financial crisis. For two years, he actively developed the code, then vanished in April 2011, leaving behind 1.1 million bitcoins (worth ~$80 billion today) untouched. The investigation examines three primary suspects: - Hal Finney (early Bitcoin developer with ALS) - Nick Szabo (created BitGold precursor) - Adam Back (invented Hashcash) In April 2026, the *New York Times* published an extensive investigation by John Carrero naming Adam Back as the most likely candidate based on stylometric analysis of 134,000 messages. However, significant contradictions emerge: Back showed minimal interest in Bitcoin for years, posted novice questions in 2013, and never accessed Satoshi\'s vast fortune. The video concludes that Satoshi\'s anonymity may be intentional and beneficial-keeping Bitcoin decentralized without a vulnerable founder figure that governments could pressure or control.',
