    level: 'advanced',
    content: 'Spark is a Bitcoin upper-layer protocol built around statechain-style transfers, shared signing and service providers. Its goal is to make bitcoin and Lightning payments easier for wallets and applications by moving frequent state updates off-chain while preserving an exit path back to Bitcoin L1. Key points: Spark transfers the right to spend Bitcoin-linked value off-chain instead of publishing every payment on-chain. Users keep a key, while a Spark Entity / operator set participates in signing and state transitions. Spark can abstract Lightning channel management for end users through service providers and swaps. Its main trade-off is not pure custody, but dependence on operators for liveness, key deletion / state integrity and transaction privacy. Spark should be treated as a pragmatic scaling layer with explicit trust assumptions, not as equivalent to direct on-chain self-custody.',
